  "qualification_basis": "Commissioned SoX-ng 14.8.0.1 response measurements, corrected PB+TW/2 profile semantics, pinned source locks, content-addressed stereo and six-channel DST oracle pairs, independent standards-literal raw-frame oracle, strict loudnorm parser, conservative 0.110000000 dB analyzer upper-error allowance, deterministic RIFF upper-bound proof, mandatory post-final acceptance measurement, and decoded-sample identity before and after metadata mutation, and explicit WavPack Int24 raw-depth declaration to prevent FFmpeg from promoting the qualified 24-bit terminal stream to 32-bit storage. The immutable cell contract expands to 53760 enabled source/rate/channel/profile/target/depth/compression/gain-mode combinations; its canonical digest is bound below.",
  "runtime_activation": "Require the runner path, activation path, and compiled Nix-store executable path to canonicalize to the same policy-owned SoX-ng/FFmpeg object. Validate embedded source locks, exact version, executable SHA-256, compiled store/package identity, behavior probes, in-process decoder source and fixture identities, platform ABI, runtime dispatch, qualification digest, and semantic plan before rerun admission or execution; fail closed without substitution.",
